  "prompt_text": "The figure presents a conceptual framework for building a “digital twin of Earth” by combining several AI approaches rather than relying on deep learning alone. At the center is the digital twin, shown as a realistic globe overlapping with a pixelated version, suggesting a bridge between the real Earth system and its computational representation.\n\nFour methods feed into this goal. Deep learning sits at the bottom as a general foundation. Physics-informed machine learning adds physical constraints, helping models respect known laws and improving transferability to new situations. Causal inference contributes interpretability by identifying cause-and-effect relationships instead of only correlations. Deep reinforcement learning adds decision-making ability through an agent–environment loop involving actions, states, and rewards.\n\nThe arrows indicate that these approaches are interconnected: deep learning supports the other methods, and each contributes a specific strength to the Earth digital twin. Overall, the message is that an effective Earth system digital twin should be physically grounded, causally understandable, transferable across conditions, and capable of supporting decisions, with these capabilities emerging from the integration of modern machine learning techniques.",
